minios-session-manager (1.2.1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Reject partial rsync transfers when copying or converting sessions so
    incomplete session trees are never published as successful copies.
  * Harden the predictable /tmp size-cache directory against symlink following
    by validating and chmodding an O_NOFOLLOW directory file descriptor.
  * Use minios-gui 1.1.0 shared HeaderBar and status banner components.
  * Restore Python 3.6 GUI helper compatibility by using universal-newline
    subprocess pipes instead of the Python 3.7-only text keyword.
  * Use shared manager row sizing and active-first status accents consistent
    with Kernel Manager.
  * Add fail-closed SquashFS saving through savechanges exact capture.
  * Build each save under a private temporary name, verify its identity, size,
    SquashFS header, digest, and extraction footprint, then atomically replace
    the current changes.sb without retaining a rollback generation.
  * Reject SquashFS saving on storage that cannot preserve exact staging
    metadata until a metadata-capable workspace is available.
  * Create and activate SquashFS snapshots with manual or automatic-at-shutdown
    save policy, while keeping Save Now available for the running session.
  * Show a desktop save icon for the running SquashFS session and a progress
    window during forced saves.
  * Delegate running SquashFS saves to the MiniOS Tools backend; shutdown
    saving no longer depends on Session Manager being installed.
  * Require MiniOS Tools 1.6.0 for the shared SquashFS save backend and exact
    capture across preserved post-switch-root module mount aliases.
  * Create the persistence guard runtime directory before systemd applies its
    read-write sandbox so the desktop SquashFS save indicator can start.
  * Improve SquashFS save UX with phase-aware delayed progress, quick-save and
    first-use desktop notifications, and shutdown output matching MiniOS teardown.
  * Add independent automatic-at-shutdown and periodic save controls in the GTK
    manager and tray, with a 30-minute minimum and explicit storage-write warning.
  * Register the persistence guard on SysV systems and add a Devuan periodic-save
    worker that performs the same 30-minute due checks as the systemd timer.
  * Show SquashFS logical snapshot size and saved time in session rows instead of
    compressed artifact size and directory timestamps.
  * Allow a running unpacked SquashFS session to hand off to a snapshot captured
    and activated during the current boot before deleting the old snapshot.
  * Warn after an unclean SquashFS boot and restore the last successfully saved
    snapshot without inventing a rollback generation.

 -- crims0n <crims0n@minios.dev>  Mon, 10 Aug 2026 00:29:10 +0300

minios-session-manager (1.2.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Add LUKS2-encrypted ext4 session containers with secure passphrase handling,
    capability-gated CLI and GUI choices, and support for creation, import,
    export, copy, conversion, and grow-only resize.
  * Add cryptsetup as a dependency and accept decimal MB, GB, and TB container
    sizes up to 1 TB, with FAT32 size limits where applicable.
  * Improve validation and data safety for session IDs, target filesystems,
    free-space checks, archive imports, export destinations, and cleanup input.
  * Preserve overlay whiteouts during session operations and support conversion
    with --new-session without replacing the source session.
  * Allow long-running GUI operations to complete without a fixed timeout,
    preserve export ownership for the invoking user, and refresh the interface
    with compact centered actions and theme-aware styling.
  * Update command-line documentation, completion, and translations for LUKS
    sessions and the new size syntax.

